{"builder":"Goal: one pull request that meets every line of https://github.com/o/strutil/issues/7 (add padLeft for zero-padding invoice numbers, e.g. 42 -> 00042).\n\nCurrent state: index.js (ES module) exports capitalize, slugify and truncate. README.md has sections '## capitalize(s)' and '## truncate(s, n)' but NO section for slugify, so the README line is already unmet before you start. Tests live in test/strutil.test.js and run with `npm test` (`node --test`).\n\nSteps:\n1. In index.js add and export `padLeft(s, width, fill)` with a short doc comment like the other functions. It pads s on the left with fill to width characters; when fill is not given (undefined) it uses a single space. When s.length >= width it returns s unchanged. Make sure the result is exactly width characters long (e.g. String.prototype.padStart behaves this way: padLeft('42', 5, '0') === '00042', padLeft('ab', 4) === '  ab', padLeft('abcdef', 3) === 'abcdef', padLeft('abc', 3, '0') === 'abc'). Do not change the existing functions.\n2. In README.md add a section for padLeft, e.g. '## padLeft(s, width, fill)', describing the left padding, the default space fill and that s is returned unchanged when already width characters or longer. ALSO add the missing section for slugify, e.g. '## slugify(s)' (lower case, words joined by dashes). Afterwards every function exported by index.js (capitalize, slugify, truncate, padLeft, plus anything else you export) must have its own '## name(...)' section.\n3. In test/strutil.test.js import padLeft and add tests: zero padding ('42', 5, '0' -> '00042'), default space fill, s exactly width long unchanged, s longer than width unchanged.\n4. Run `npm test` and make sure it passes with 0 failures. Then open the pull request.","verifier":"Check the pull request head for issue https://github.com/o/strutil/issues/7. Run everything from the repository root at the PR head. One check per expect line, in order.\n\nCheck 1 — expect: \"index.js exports padLeft(s, width, fill), which pads s on the left with fill (a space when fill is not given) to width characters\"\nRun: node --input-type=module -e \"import * as m from './index.js'; console.log(typeof m.padLeft); console.log(JSON.stringify([m.padLeft('42',5,'0'), m.padLeft('ab',4), m.padLeft('7',3,'x')]))\"\nPASS: typeof is 'function' and the outputs are [\"00042\",\"  ab\",\"xx7\"] (padded on the left with the given fill, or a space when fill is omitted, to exactly width characters).\nFAIL: padLeft is not exported from index.js, the import throws, or any result is not left-padded with the fill/space to width characters.\n\nCheck 2 — expect: \"padLeft returns s unchanged when s is already width characters or longer\"\nRun: node --input-type=module -e \"import {padLeft} from './index.js'; console.log(JSON.stringify([padLeft('abc',3,'0'), padLeft('abcdef',3,'0'), padLeft('abcdef',3)]))\"\nPASS: output is [\"abc\",\"abcdef\",\"abcdef\"].\nFAIL: any value differs from the input s (padded, truncated or otherwise changed), or the call throws.\n\nCheck 3 — expect: \"README.md has a section for every function index.js exports\"\nRun: node --input-type=module -e \"import * as m from './index.js'; console.log(Object.keys(m).filter(k=>typeof m[k]==='function').join(' '))\" to list the exported functions, then read README.md at the head and list its section headings (lines starting with '#').\nPASS: every exported function name (this must include capitalize, slugify, truncate and padLeft) has its own README.md section whose heading names that function.\nFAIL: any exported function has no section in README.md. Note: at the base README.md had no slugify section, so a PR that only adds padLeft fails this check.\n\nCheck 4 — expect: \"npm test passes\"\nRun: npm test\nPASS: the command exits 0 and reports no failing tests.\nFAIL: non-zero exit or any failing test.\n\nAdvisory (not pass/fail conditions): it is good if test/strutil.test.js includes tests for padLeft (zero padding, default fill, s at or above width); multi-character fill behaviour is not specified by the issue."}